<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Lord, can no righteousness,</l><l>Be found upon the earth?</l><l>The tambourine and lyre,</l><l>Have ceased to bring me mirth.</l><l>Yet in Thy dwelling place,</l><l>I saw the wicked’s end.</l><l>Thy counsel guides me still,</l><l>Thou leadest by Thy hand.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>The broken, contrite heart,</l><l>Is ne’er despised by Thee;</l><l>My many wicked sins</l><l>Have henceforth humbled me!</l><l>The sinner’s vile offense,</l><l>To God’s forgiveness wed,</l><l>Brings forth the builded work;</l><l>To Zion thus I’m led.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
